s that the brief says should be included or\n     referenced in the email body.\n\n4. Build the campaign audience in Salesforce CRM. You MUST use an exhaustive\n   fallback strategy before concluding there are no recipients:\n\n   a) Search BOTH Leads and Contacts modules.\n\n   b) Start with strict title/role filters based on the brief:\n      - CTO, CIO, VP Engineering, VP IT, IT Director, Head of Digital, Head of Data.\n\n   c) If that returns few or no results, you MUST broaden your search iteratively\n      using additional Technology-related keywords in titles, departments, or tags,\n      such as:\n      - "Technology", "Tech", "IT", "Information Technology", "Engineering",\n        "Software", "Infrastructure", "Operations", "DevOps", "Cloud",\n        "Digital", "Data", "Analytics", "Security", "Cyber", "Platform",\n        "Architecture", "Architect".\n\n   d) For each broadened search:\n      - Query Leads with those keywords.\n      - Query Contacts with those keywords.\n      - Collect all matching records that have a valid work email address.\n\n   e) Deduplicate by email address so each recipient only appears once.\n\n   f) You should continue broadening and combining reasonable Technology-adjacent\n      roles until you have at least some non-empty set of recipients with valid\n      work emails or you have exhausted obvious keyword combinations. Do NOT stop\n      at the first empty result; always expand your search terms before giving up.\n\n   The result of this step should be a final list of one or more Technology-aligned\n   leads and/or contacts with valid email addresses. If you find any such records,\n   you MUST proceed to send the campaign to them.\n\n5. Prepare and send the campaign:\n   - From: Emma’s usual marketing sender identity.\n   - Subject: exactly as specified in the brief for this Technology/Q2 pilot\n     (for example, “Exclusive Investment Opportunity for Corporate Partners” if\n     that is what the brief states).\n   - Body: